from lesson_writer import author,CPP
author('src/org/minima/objects/mmr/MegaMMR.md','Maintains an MMR plus an identifier-indexed set of unspent coins, with optional aggressive pruning.',[
 'addBlock applies previous peaks, spent-input proofs and new output leaves to the current MMR. Spent coin IDs are removed from the unspent table; output deep copies get fresh entry numbers and creation heights before insertion.',
 'Prunability is a configured policy: when mega-pruning is enabled, a non-32-byte address qualifies, and optional flags also qualify coins with state or non-Minima token IDs. This is a policy decision, not execution of the coin’s script.',
 'After applying a block, compare the computed root with the TxPoW root. A mismatch logs a message; it does not reject the block, roll back changes or return false.',
 'Scanning updates leaf unspendable flags from current coin policy. Tree pruning records removed entry numbers, and a replacement coin table retains only coins not in that pruned set.',
 'Writing can mutate the object: when enabled, it prunes before writing version 1, MMR and coins in Java Hashtable enumeration order. Thus serialization is not a pure observation.',
 'Reading consumes but does not validate version, replaces the MMR/table, clears MMR finalization, loads coins by ID and rescans/prunes using current settings. Duplicate IDs overwrite earlier table entries.',
 'clear replaces both structures. isEmpty checks stored MMR entries rather than the unspent-coin count, so an empty coin table alone is insufficient.'
], 'C++ reuses applyBlockMMR for the same state transition as tree nodes and JavaHashtable for observable coin iteration. MMR and coins have shared ownership; the table container itself is assigned in place, which can differ from Java retained-table aliases after replacement. Log output currently uses std::clog rather than the full Java logger.',
 lambda l:'The '+l(CPP/'support/ObjectOracle.java','object oracle')+' and '+l(CPP/'support/objects.cpp','native harness')+' build MegaMMRs over one or three rounds, spend every third eligible entry in later rounds and optionally prune after each block. The '+l(CPP/'tools/object_differential.py','driver')+' combines eight output sizes, sixteen flag settings and two round counts, plus empty state: 257 initial MegaMMR fixtures, then derived read/trailing/truncation cases. Wire bytes, MMR JSON, coin JSON/order and emptiness are compared. The existing object report has 9,244 passing total comparisons; this is a whole-suite count. Java fixture logs are suppressed, so root-mismatch logging is not verified there.',
 'Why could calling serialise reduce getAllCoins().size()? Explain which configuration causes it and why a test must snapshot state after writing as well as compare bytes.',
 'Policy changes between creation/read/write, retained table aliases, logger/error fidelity and arbitrary file failures remain open. A matching root fixture does not prove full consensus validation: this method only logs mismatches. Partial counterpart, parity not_verified.')
author('src/org/minima/objects/IBD.md','Packages initial block-download data: an optional cascade followed by ordered TxBlocks, with logic for selecting the portion a peer needs.',[
 'A complete IBD deep-copies the current cascade but shares TxBlock references from the tree, arranged root-to-tip. Setters themselves simply retain supplied cascade/list references; their comments do not guarantee deep copies.',
 'createIBD returns true immediately if the local tree is empty. Otherwise it locks reads. A peer with top -1 gets a complete IBD; overlapping chains get blocks after the first greeting-chain ID found locally.',
 'For a peer behind the local root, search archive IDs at every twentieth greeting entry, then the final entry if still unmatched. An intersection at most 34,000 blocks behind prepends archive data and the current tree; missing/too-distant intersections fall back to a complete snapshot.',
 'Overlapping ranges with no matching ID set the returned validity flag false, yet still create a complete IBD. Caught exceptions log and can leave partial state while returning the flag’s previous value. Several incremental paths append to existing lists rather than clearing them.',
 'Sync mode clears the cascade and appends an archive range after a shutdown check. Archive mode can load a stored cascade when starting at zero, requests the open interval (start-1, start+256), and optionally appends the current main tree when its root matches the request.',
 'checkValidData only adds checks when a nonempty cascade exists: blocks must exist, first height must equal cascade tip plus one, and cascade consistency must pass. It does not validate every transaction or block linkage.',
 'Total weight sums block decimals and truncates that sum to an integer, separately truncates cascade weight, then adds. Chain comparison seeks crossover in tree/tree, tree/cascade, cascade/tree, cascade/cascade precedence, shortens both including the intersection and favors our chain on equal weight.',
 'Wire format is a MiniByte presence flag, optional cascade, count and blocks. Reads replace the block list and retain any decoded prefix on later failure. Java catches OutOfMemoryError only inside the block-writing loop, after writing the declared count.'
], 'Native IBD retains shared cascade/list/block ownership and reuses Cascade, TxBlock, MiniNumber and exact BigInt weight arithmetic. Required IBDServices callbacks represent database, archive, shutdown and lock access. checkChains is a native pure adapter used after the source-equivalent current snapshot. Standard exceptions/logging and allocation behavior still need separate fidelity review.',
 lambda l:'The '+l(CPP/'support/IBDOracle.java','Java IBD oracle')+', '+l(CPP/'support/ibd.cpp','native harness')+' and '+l(CPP/'tools/ibd_differential.py','driver')+' compare complete/greeting/sync/archive paths, preloaded state, empty/bad cascades, shortening/crossover order, archive sampling positions, query parameters, shutdown/fault paths and lock depth. Derived wire cases inspect consumed offsets, cascade presence and partial block counts. The inspected '+l(CPP/'build/ibd-differential-results.json','report')+' has 1,057 matching cases. Java Main construction is bypassed; controlled archive and lock receivers make these offline behavioral tests.',
 'A peer claims an overlapping height range but shares no IDs. Why can createIBD return false while the object still contains a complete download? Which two observations must your test assert?',
 'No real network synchronization or database persistence is established. Generic errors/logs and out-of-memory stack printing are not compared; the native bad_alloc catch does not prove equivalent allocation timing. Null cascades can still fail comparison/printing APIs even though the wire permits absence. Partial counterpart, parity not_verified.')
